From 5012e994a6c7617d869b7d20398213122df7582f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:41:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: per-draw values in a uniform binding on older Adreno
 Vulkan; adapter capabilities and fallbacks logged

On Adreno before the 730 (the 710 of the Snapdragon 6 Gen 1 and 7s Gen 2,
the 6xx) under Vulkan, draws with indexed vertex arrays (maps, models)
vanished and only 2D drew (backgrounds, text boxes) once the per-draw values
(vtx_start, array_start) moved into immediates (push constants). Those
devices now take the uniform-binding path the web build already has (and
Aurora used before immediates); native builds decide it at device creation
instead of assuming immediates. $AURORA_NO_IMMEDIATES=1 forces the fallback
anywhere, $AURORA_IMMEDIATES=1 keeps immediates on such an Adreno.

Startup now logs the adapter's ids, every feature it offers and the limits
GX rendering leans on, and one line of the fallbacks chosen (compatibility
mode, BC and R8/RG8 decoded on the CPU, no dual-source blending, uniform
binding). The vertex and storage buffers are capped at the device's storage
binding size rather than assumed to fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
